Subject: [PATCH next 0056] thunderbolt: gpu_stream: writable-RX admission and a no-traffic PREFLIGHT

An RX import maps a DMA-BUF that the controller then writes, but the
import did not check that the exporter granted write access: a DMA-BUF
file opened read-only was accepted. Refuse it with EACCES in the shared
window mapper, so IMPORT and the new PREFLIGHT apply the same rule. KFD
exports a writable allocation O_RDWR, so ordinary engine buffers pass.

Add SGU_IOC_PREFLIGHT: it maps one buffer through exactly the validator
IMPORT uses (identity, size, write access for RX, SG coverage, frame
containment, DMA mask, TX/RX aliasing), reports aggregate geometry only
(SG entries, mapped bytes, min/max segment, ring frames) and releases the
mapping before returning. It changes no ring, descriptor, path or import
state and is refused once the context is armed or started. Advertised as
SGU_CAP_PREFLIGHT through SGU_IOC_QUEUE; abi_minor stays 0 (additive,
like the terminal header).

---
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/gpu_stream.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/gpu_stream.c
@@ -660,6 +660,13 @@
     if (w->buffer->size != b->full_bytes || huge_encode_dev(inode->i_sb->s_dev) != b->fd_device ||
         inode->i_ino != b->fd_inode)
         goto fail;
+    /* The controller writes RX payloads: the exporter must have granted write
+     * access (a DMA-BUF file opened for writing, e.g. KFD exports a writable
+     * allocation O_RDWR). */
+    if (direction == SGU_DIRECTION_RX && !(w->buffer->file->f_mode & FMODE_WRITE)) {
+        ret = -EACCES;
+        goto fail;
+    }
     if (direction == SGU_DIRECTION_RX && ctx->windows[SGU_DIRECTION_TX].buffer &&
         (w->buffer == ctx->windows[SGU_DIRECTION_TX].buffer ||
          w->buffer->resv == ctx->windows[SGU_DIRECTION_TX].buffer->resv))
@@ -1424,6 +1431,43 @@
